========== MANUAL ### 6. Capture APEX source as an operator ==========
### 6. Capture APEX source as an operator

- Leave SQLcl with Ctrl+D. In the same terminal create a new staging directory; the capture does not overwrite the source checkout:

  ```bash
  mkdir -p .local-apex/captures/foundation-operator-review
  sql -nohistory -noupdates -home "$APEX_CICD_CONNECTIONS" -name lab-dev
  ```

- At the SQLcl prompt, verify the target and reservation, select its workspace and run the native export as separate operations:

  ```sql
  @deploy/operator/identity.sql E1_DEV_A E1_DEV_A
  @deploy/operator/assert_ownership.sql Foundation foundation-initial 1
  begin
    apex_util.set_workspace('E1_DEV_A');
  end;
  /
  @deploy/operator/application_inventory.sql
  apex export -applicationid 810001 -split -skipExportDate -expOriginalIds -expSupportingObjects N -dir .local-apex/captures/foundation-operator-review
  ```

- Stop if identity/ownership fails or inventory does not show application 810001 in E1_DEV_A.
- Export should report the workspace and creation of f810001/install.sql.
- The flags request split source, omit the changing export timestamp, retain original component IDs and exclude supporting-object installation.
- Database changes are managed separately by the changelog.
- Leave SQLcl before returning to shell commands.

